      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically 850 mg three times daily. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg** per dose, if a different strength was intended\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note that it was verified as intentional."
      }
